	<description>There is no more authoritative collection of the poetry that Eliot himself wished to preserve than this volume, published two years before his death in 1965.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Poet, dramatist, critic, and editor, T. S. Eliot was one of the defining figures of twentieth-century poetry. This edition of Collected Poems 1909-1962 includes his verse from Prufrock and Other Observations (1917) to Four Quartets (1943), and includes such literary landmarks as The Waste Land and Old Possum's Book of Practical Cats.</description>
